init.description:
In your MCP client, choose Streamable HTTP. Paste one of the addresses below as the server URL, and send the header `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN` using the add-on's bearer token.

**Recommended (headers and streaming work):** {remote_ui_url}

**Cloud webhook:** {cloudhook_url}

Local path, appended to any Home Assistant address: `{local_path}`

The cloud webhook may drop request headers, so the client cannot send the bearer token that way. Turn the option below on only if that is the case. The cloud webhook address then acts as the secret, and Home Assistant adds the token for you. A wrong token is still rejected. The remote address always requires the token.
